00:10:07.617 --> 00:10:08.950
MELANIE WARRICK: We're done now.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:10.630
Last question I want
to ask you both is,

00:10:10.630 --> 00:10:12.760
coming from this program,
is there any advice

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:15.800
that you have for those
who are getting into tech?

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.800
STEPHANIE CUETO: So at
the end of our last week,

00:10:17.800 --> 00:10:18.550
Michelle made us--

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:21.130
Michelle, the CEO, she
made us reflect and write

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:24.190
down advice that you probably
have for future apprentices.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.780
And I kind of
thought about myself,

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:27.190
and I was like,
what would I want

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:29.237
to hear in the beginning
of this program

00:10:29.237 --> 00:10:31.570
to make it a little bit easier
and everything like that?

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:33.170
And so we did write
down a couple of things.

00:10:33.170 --> 00:10:35.680
And one of those things to me
was, or to the future ones,

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:39.010
is like, hey, this is going
to be tough, so make sure

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.840
you do prepare.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.910
Make sure you're strict
with your schedule.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.455
You are going to have to
really focus right now.

00:10:46.455 --> 00:10:48.080
You're going to have
to be frugal, too,

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:49.120
because it's a long process.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:50.420
You're not working right now.

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.620
And so make sure that you're
very disciplined, one.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:55.120
It's OK to say no.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:58.286
It's OK to say no to other
activities, like birthdays,

00:10:58.286 --> 00:10:59.410
like all these festivities.

00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:01.326
They're going to be there
still the next year.

00:11:01.326 --> 00:11:03.411
And so right now, you
need to focus on you.

00:11:03.411 --> 00:11:05.410
And that was the one main
thing that I was like,

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:06.840
it's OK to say no.

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:08.470
And it's OK to focus on this.

00:11:08.470 --> 00:11:12.160
And you need to be a
little bit selfish.

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:14.050
You just need to focus
on yourself right now.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:15.640
MELANIE WARRICK: That's great.

00:11:15.640 --> 00:11:18.760
VIVIAN SAN: And I would
say it's OK to feel scared,

00:11:18.760 --> 00:11:21.010
because I went into it
and I was so terrified.

00:11:21.010 --> 00:11:22.900
I was like, I
don't know anything

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:24.250
and I don't know what to expect.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.611
And everything was
just so unknown.

00:11:26.611 --> 00:11:28.610
I think I would just tell
the future apprentices

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:30.880
that it's OK to feel scared.

00:11:30.880 --> 00:11:33.490
And I think just allowing
yourself to feel vulnerable,

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:34.615
and the fact that
you do feel scared,

00:11:34.615 --> 00:11:36.448
I think that's actually
a really good thing,

00:11:36.448 --> 00:11:38.350
because it's telling
you that you're actually

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:40.269
trying to push yourself
to learn something new

00:11:40.269 --> 00:11:41.560
and trying to change your life.

00:11:41.560 --> 00:11:42.390
And I think that's OK.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:43.848
Like you feel scared
might actually

00:11:43.848 --> 00:11:45.657
be a good thing,
especially if there is--

00:11:45.657 --> 00:11:47.740
more cohorts that are
coming in, I would tell them

00:11:47.740 --> 00:11:50.510
that we need more women
and we need more diversity,

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:51.700
we need more inclusion.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.710
And by doing this,
you are helping

00:11:54.710 --> 00:11:57.910
to, I guess, as Michelle would
say, bridge the tech gap.

00:11:57.910 --> 00:12:00.130
Essentially, just
being able to put more

00:12:00.130 --> 00:12:01.240
perspectives out there.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:03.580
And you are going
to be someone who's

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:06.187
going to be part of this
community to change the world.

00:12:06.187 --> 00:12:08.020
STEPHANIE CUETO: I think
I would add on to--

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:08.710
MELANIE WARRICK: Yeah, please.

00:12:08.710 --> 00:12:09.640
STEPHANIE CUETO:
--you are like--

00:12:09.640 --> 00:12:11.060
we all became very close.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:11.810
We're very strong.

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:14.320
And it's like make sure--

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.300
you are all going
through similar things,

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:18.600
reach out to one another,
speak to one another.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:19.975
You're going to
go through a lot.

00:12:19.975 --> 00:12:21.940
And so make sure you
have that support system,

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:24.589
because maybe your parents or
anyone doesn't really know what

00:12:24.589 --> 00:12:25.880
you're going through right now.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:28.570
It's a different background,
or maybe even friends.

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:31.180
So you guys are all going
to become very strong.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.715
And make sure you keep
that together and rely

00:12:33.715 --> 00:12:34.340
on one another.

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:35.580
MELANIE WARRICK:
Find your community.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.630
Build your community.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.755
And places like this, too,
give you the opportunity

00:12:38.755 --> 00:12:39.930
to expand that too.

00:12:39.930 --> 00:12:40.420
STEPHANIE CUETO: Yeah.

